WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.187
The applied challenge combines the module.

00:00:02.187 --> 00:00:04.407
Return one row per admission.

00:00:04.407 --> 00:00:06.672
Create a normalized patient name.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:11.252
Extract the email domain while preserving admissions for patients with missing email.

00:00:11.252 --> 00:00:13.367
Create an admission month bucket.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.762
Add a human-readable admission label.

00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:18.217
Calculate length of stay in hours.

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:26.347
Build and test one output column at a time instead of trying to finish the entire SELECT immediately.

00:00:26.347 --> 00:00:29.072
Connect this idea to an operations team aligning timestamps across locations.

00:00:29.072 --> 00:00:36.072
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:36.072 --> 00:00:41.182
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.182 --> 00:00:46.402
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:46.402 --> 00:00:51.755
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
